    brand: "Matrix",
    category: "Commercial AC Treadmill From Vision’s Parent Company",
    badge: "Closest on Amazon to the T600",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07YGMKD52?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41V75z6TXyL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":416},
    reviewUrl: "/matrix-t5x-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "$3,999-$4,399 remanufactured (one US reseller, 14 Oct 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":3999,"high":4399},
    specs: "60 in. running length · 5.0 HP AC drive · 0.5-12 mph · 0-15% incline · non-folding · dedicated 20 A circuit",
    pros: [
      "A 5.0 HP AC drive built for club use, agreed across Matrix’s manual and reseller listings",
      "Incline to 15% and a full 60-inch running length",
      "Simple LED console with no subscription or platform to go out of date",
      "Remanufactured units come with a reseller warranty that can include on-site labour",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Not on Matrix’s US home store, so a new one with a Matrix residential warranty is not the realistic option",
      "Width, user-weight rating and machine weight conflict across sources and generations",
      "Needs a dedicated 20-amp circuit with a matching outlet on a 120-volt supply",
      "Heavy, long and non-folding; delivery and access need planning",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The nearest Amazon alternative to a T600: a Johnson Health Tech club AC treadmill, bought remanufactured with a written warranty, if your room has a 20-amp circuit.",
    description: "The T5x is a Matrix commercial treadmill sold under the same name in at least an older and a newer style. Matrix’s owner’s manual for the MX-T5x and independent reseller listings agree on a 5.0 HP AC drive, a 60-inch running length, 0 to 15% incline, a speed range of 0.5 to 12 mph and a 20-amp electrical requirement (NEMA 5-20 on 120 volts). They disagree on the rest. The manual gives a 22-inch-wide running area, a 500 lb maximum user weight and 450 lb machine weight; one reseller’s chart gives 20 inches wide and 400 lb for both styles; another listing gives a 22-inch belt, 400 lb, 399 lb machine weight and a 15 mph top speed. A US remanufacturer listed the older style at $3,999 and the newer style at $4,399 on 14 October 2026, with a one-year parts and on-site labour warranty and extended options. We could not confirm it is sold new by Matrix in the US. It sits on this page in place of the Vision T600, which Vision sells only through its own offices and dealers. Matrix and Vision are both Johnson Health Tech brands, and the T5x is the closest light-commercial AC treadmill from that family we could find on Amazon US.",
  },
  {
    id: "nordictrack-commercial-2450",
    name: "NordicTrack Commercial 2450",
    brand: "NordicTrack",
    category: "Touchscreen Treadmill With a 400 lb Rating",
    badge: "Touchscreen Alternative on Amazon",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D5YKDXDV?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31NVjoFCMQL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $2,299 (Amazon, 6 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":2299,"high":2299},
    specs: "22 x 60 in. belt · 4.25 CHP (NordicTrack rating) · 0–14 mph · -3% to 12% incline · 400 lb max user · folds",
