    bottomLine: "For a buyer drawn to the T600E's touchscreen who wants a 22-inch deck and 400 lb rating for a fraction of the price, and will use iFIT.",
    description: "The Commercial 2450 is NordicTrack's folding flagship, and on paper it matches the T600E's 22 by 60-inch deck and 400 lb rating with a large touchscreen. NordicTrack lists a 22 by 60-inch belt, a 4.25 CHP motor by its own continuous rating and a 400 lb maximum user weight, and the Amazon listing gives a 0–14 mph speed range, a -3% to 12% incline, RunFlex cushioning, a 24-inch touchscreen that tilts and pivots, and a folding frame with assisted lowering. The 400 lb rating is the highest of the established-brand machines here, and the 14 mph top speed is the fastest. The trade-off is that much of the price goes into the screen and its software: the listing describes the full experience with an iFIT Pro membership, which iFIT listed at $39 a month in November 2026. The treadmill runs without it, in manual mode. Amazon listed it at $2,299 on 6 November 2026. It takes the place of the Vision T600E on this page, which is sold only through Vision dealers: it is a home folding treadmill rather than a light-commercial machine, so it is the alternative for the screen and the deck, not for gym-level hours.",
  },
  {
    id: "horizon-7-4-at",
    name: "Horizon 7.4 AT",
    brand: "Horizon",
    category: "Johnson Health Tech’s Home Treadmill in Vision’s Old Price Band",
    badge: "Closest on Amazon",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08JQQHR7R?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
