    reviewUrl: "/life-fitness-run-cx-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "$3,919 at Life Fitness on 5 Nov 2026",
    priceBounds: {"low":3919,"high":3919},
    specs: "22 x 60 in. running surface · 3.0 HP continuous DC (6.0 HP peak) · 0.5-12 mph · 0-15% incline · 400 lb max user",
    pros: [
      "The T600’s 400 lb rating and 22 by 60-inch surface at well under the T600E’s price",
      "Lifetime frame and Lifespring cover, 10 years on the motor and 7 on parts",
      "Delivery and installation included",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A DC motor, not an AC drive",
      "Life Fitness quoted a five-to-seven-week lead time",
      "No touchscreen option",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The pick for a buyer who wants club-brand build at home without paying light-commercial prices.",
    description: "The Run CX is Life Fitness’s premium home treadmill. Life Fitness’s US store lists a 22 by 60-inch running surface, a 3.0 HP continuous (6.0 HP peak) DC motor, 0.5 to 12 mph, 0 to 15% incline and a 400 lb maximum user weight, which our review cross-checked against an authorised dealer, with lifetime frame and Lifespring cover, 10 years on the motor, 7 on parts, 3 on the console and 1 on labour. On 5 November 2026 it was $3,919, down from $4,899, with delivery and installation.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Brands", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/brands/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Vision Fitness Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/vision-fitness-treadmills/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Vision Fitness still make treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, but only one on its US site on 5 November 2026: the light-commercial T600, with an LED console or as the T600E with a 22-inch touchscreen, sold through dealers. The home models such as the TF20, T40, T80 and T9200 are no longer listed; the recall notice says the recalled home models were sold until May 2025.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Who owns Vision Fitness?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Johnson Health Tech, the Taiwanese group that also owns Horizon, Matrix, Bowflex and Schwinn Fitness. Johnson Health Tech North America is the firm named on the 2026 Vision treadmill recall.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is a Vision T600 treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Vision publishes no price. On 5 November 2026 Fitness Supply, a US dealer, listed the touchscreen T600E at $8,799. Earlier US listings put the LED T600 at about $5,400, which we could not confirm on the day. Prices vary by dealer and region.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What are the Vision T600 specs?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Vision and a US dealer agree on a 4.2 HP AC drive, a 22 by 60-inch running surface, 0.5 to 12 mph on 120 V, 0 to 15% incline, a 400 lb user limit, 85 by 36 by 65 inches and 408 lb. It does not fold.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the Vision T9200 a good treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It was a basic home treadmill from the 2000s, with figures that vary by version: about 2.5 HP, 12 mph, 12% incline and 325 lb for the basic model in one review, and 3.0 CHP for the Deluxe. Any T9200 is now around 20 years old; buy one only for very little and expect to source parts from third parties.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Which Vision treadmills were recalled?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "In January 2026 Johnson Health Tech recalled about 47,000 Matrix Retail and Vision treadmills, including the Vision T9800, TF20, T40 and T80 made from 2007 to January 2024, because the power cord can work loose and overheat. The remedy is a free locking power cord. A 2006 recall covered about 480 Premier consoles.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What replaced Vision home treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Johnson Health Tech’s other home brands. The Horizon 7.8 AT, $1,999 on 5 November 2026, has a 22 by 60-inch deck, 15% incline and 375 lb rating; Matrix covers the premium dealer market Vision’s top home models sold into.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-05",
      dateModified: "2026-11-05",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 4,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/vision-fitness-treadmills/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/vision-fitness-treadmills/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "brands");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-05",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-05",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "vision fitness treadmill",
      "treadmill vision fitness",
      "vision fitness t600 treadmill",
      "vision fitness treadmill t9200",
      "vision t600e treadmill",
      "vision treadmill recall",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Closest on Amazon to the T600: Matrix T5x", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/brands/">Brands</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buyer’s Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Vision Fitness Treadmills: The T600 Today, and the Home Models Before It</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        Vision Fitness, a Johnson Health Tech brand, used to sell a full line of home treadmills through specialty dealers — the T9200, T9800, TF20, T40 and T80 among them. Its US site now lists one treadmill, the light-commercial T600 with an LED or touchscreen console, and directs buyers to a local Vision office. Here is what the T600 is and costs, what the old home models were, which of them are in the January 2026 recall, and where to look instead.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 5, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#matrix-t5x"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41V75z6TXyL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Matrix T5x" width="500" height="416" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#nordictrack-commercial-2450"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31NVjoFCMQL._SL500_.jpg" alt="NordicTrack Commercial 2450" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#horizon-7-4-at"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41wMaZFsNwL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Horizon 7.4 AT" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Matrix T5x · NordicTrack Commercial 2450 · Horizon 7.4 AT</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          For twenty years "Vision Fitness" meant a particular kind of treadmill: sold through specialty fitness
          stores rather than big-box retailers, a step above department-store brands in build and warranty, and
          made by the same company as Horizon and Matrix. Searches still reflect that, for the T9200 in particular.
          But the line has changed. Vision's US website now presents the brand as a supplier to facilities —
          gyms, apartment buildings, corporate fitness centres — and its catalogue lists a single treadmill, the
          T600. The older home treadmills are no longer listed, and four of them were recalled in January 2026 for
          a loose power cord. This guide covers the T600 as a home purchase, what the older models were, how to
          check a used one, and the Johnson Health Tech home treadmills that now fill Vision's old role.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon to the T600:</span> <a href="#matrix-t5x">Matrix T5x</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Touchscreen Alternative on Amazon:</span> <a href="#nordictrack-commercial-2450">NordicTrack Commercial 2450</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon:</span> <a href="#horizon-7-4-at">Horizon 7.4 AT</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Premium Home Pick:</span> <a href="#life-fitness-run-cx">Life Fitness Run CX</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we checked Vision Fitness's US site (its home page, cardio catalogue and the T600/T600E
          product page), Fitness Supply's US listing for the T600E with its warranty terms, other US, Canadian,
          Australian and UK dealer listings for the T600 seen in search results, TreadmillReviews.com and Treadmill
          Doctor coverage of the T9200 and manuals and parts listings for older models, the US Consumer Product Safety
          Commission's recall database for Vision Fitness and Johnson Health Tech (recall 26-203 of January 2026 and
          recall 06-556 of 2006), and Horizon's and Life Fitness's US stores for the alternatives, as checked for our
          reviews of those machines the same day. On 9 November 2026 we replaced the T600 and T600E cards with the
          Matrix T5x and NordicTrack Commercial 2450, which are sold on Amazon; their figures are those checked for our
          Matrix T5x review and heavy-duty treadmill guide. The same day the Horizon 7.8 AT card became the Horizon 7.4 AT,
          which Amazon sells, with the figures checked for our Horizon treadmill guide. Vision publishes no prices; the T600E price is one dealer's, and
          dealer prices vary by region and change often. Conflicting figures are set out in the text and kept off the
          cards. We have not tested any Vision treadmill. As an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases;
          that does not change what we say.
        </aside>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this guide">
          <h2>In this guide</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-is-vision">Who Makes Vision Fitness Treadmills?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#t600">The T600</a></li>
            <li><a href="#older-models">Older Models</a></li>
            <li><a href="#recalls">The 2026 Recall</a></li>
            <li><a href="#alternatives">What to Buy Instead of a Vision Home Treadmill</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Does Vision Fitness Still Make Home Treadmills? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Not as it used to. On 5 November 2026 Vision Fitness's US site listed one treadmill, the
            light-commercial T600 (or T600E with a touchscreen), sold through dealers with no published price. The
            older home models, including the T9200 and the T40, T80 and TF20, are no longer listed, and several are in
            a January 2026 recall.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            The T600 is a serious machine: a 4.2 HP AC drive, a 22 by 60-inch running surface, 15% incline and a 400 lb
            rating, figures Vision and a US dealer agree on. It is also non-folding, weighs 408 lb and, as a T600E,
            cost $8,799 at the one US dealer price we could confirm. That puts it in a different category from the
            Vision home treadmills people remember.
          </p>
          <p>
            For most homes, Vision's own parent company is the better place to look: the <a href="/horizon-7-8-at-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Horizon 7.8 AT</a> has the same deck
            size and incline with a 375 lb rating for $1,999. If you are buying a used Vision, check its model and serial
            number against the recall before anything else. We have not tested any Vision treadmill.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-is-vision" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Who Makes Vision Fitness Treadmills?</h2>
<p>
            Vision Fitness is a brand of Johnson Health Tech, the Taiwanese group that also owns Horizon, Matrix, <a href="/bowflex/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Bowflex</a> and Schwinn Fitness. Vision's site is built on Johnson Health Tech's asset servers, and the January
            2026 recall names Johnson Health Tech North America as the firm responsible for Vision treadmills.
          </p>
          <p>
            Historically, the brands had distinct jobs. Horizon sold to general retail, Matrix covered commercial clubs
            and, later, premium home machines, and Vision sat between them: home treadmills such as the TF20, T40 and
            T80 sold through specialty fitness dealers, plus light-commercial equipment. The recall notice lists Vision
            among the brands sold through dealers including G&amp;G Fitness, Fitness Expo and Treadmill Outlet, and
            online at visionfitness.com, from 2012 until May 2025.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What Vision sells now</h3>
          <p>
            Vision's US site now describes treadmills built to handle high-traffic environments and addresses gyms,
            health clubs, corporate gyms and multifamily housing. Alongside the T600 it lists ellipticals, bikes, the
            Summit cardio series and selectorized, plate-loaded and free-weight strength equipment, and asks buyers to
            contact a local Vision office rather than buy online. It does not mention home use. Johnson Health Tech's
            premium home treadmills now carry the <a href="/matrix-fitness/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Matrix</a> name, and its mid-range home
            treadmills the <a href="/horizon-fitness/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Horizon</a> name.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="t600" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Vision T600 and T600E</h2>
<p>
            The T600 is one frame with two consoles. The T600 has a 10 by 14 dot-matrix LED display with a dedicated
            heart-rate zone readout; the T600E has the Entertainment console, a 22-inch touchscreen. Vision's page
            gives the same figures for both. Vision sells both only through its own offices and dealers, not on
            Amazon, so the product cards below show the nearest alternatives sold there — a Matrix T5x from the same
            parent company in the T600's place and a NordicTrack Commercial 2450 for the T600E's touchscreen — next to
            the Horizon and Life Fitness home alternatives. Horizon's 7.8 AT is sold by Horizon rather than on Amazon,
            so the Horizon card shows its sibling, the 7.4 AT. The T600 figures are in the table.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Figure</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Vision</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Fitness Supply (US dealer)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Motor</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4.2 HP AC</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4.2 HP AC</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Running surface</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">22 x 60 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">22 x 60 in.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Speed (120 V)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0.5-12 mph</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0.5-12 mph</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Incline</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0-15%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0-15%</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Max user</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">400 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">400 lb</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Size / weight</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">85 x 36 x 65 in., 408 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">85 x 36 x 65 in., 408 lb</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Conflicts we found</h3>
          <p>
            Overseas dealer listings are less consistent. One gives a 3.0 HP drive, and an Australian listing gives an
            assembled weight of 392 lb. On 220 V supplies the top speed is 13.8 mph, which explains some listings' higher
            figures. We have used Vision's and the US dealer's matching figures on the cards.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Price and warranty</h3>
          <p>
            Vision publishes no prices. Fitness Supply listed the T600E at $8,799 on 5 November 2026. A US T600ENT listing
            seen in search results showed the same figure; earlier listings put the LED T600 at about $5,400 in the US and
            $4,699 in Canada, but we could not confirm those on the day. Warranty depends on the dealer and on how the
            treadmill is used: Fitness Supply's commercial-use terms were 7 years on the frame, 5 on the motor and parts,
            2 on labour and 90 days on wear items, and another retailer page in search results showed a lifetime frame,
            5-year motor and 2-year labour term, which may be the residential version. Ask the dealer for the warranty in
            writing, for home use, before you buy.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Putting one in a home</h3>
          <p>
            Vision lists a NEMA 5-15 plug for 100-120 V supplies, the ordinary household plug shape, so a 20-amp
            circuit may not be required; ask the dealer whether a dedicated circuit is recommended. The bigger issues are
            size and weight: 85 inches long, 65 inches high and 408 lb, with no fold. Our guide to putting a <a href="/gym-treadmill-for-home/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">gym treadmill in a home</a> covers floors, stairs and access routes.
          </p>
        </div>
